+In accordance with NDEP requirements and the WPCP, and through the implementation of the Final Permanent Closure Plan, the primary goal of conducting post-mining water resources monitoring will be to demonstrate that the Project site poses no potential to degrade groundwater and surface water in the Project area. Consequently, groundwater and surface water monitoring will continue for at least three years after cessation of mine, processing, and closure operations. Furthermore, LNC does not anticipate any CTFS seepage; however, should any seepage occur, LNC will monitor the quantity and quality of this seepage. Water resources (surface water and groundwater) monitoring sites are presented on Figure 17. The Reclamation Cost Estimate (Appendix J) contains costs for at least five years of water resource monitoring.
 
